raud and DEI controversies have given Republicans an opening in a D+3 state"], "rationale": "The polling average has compressed to roughly +2 for Flanagan, and headlines point to a genuine late tightening driven by fraud and DEI attacks, but expert ratings remain mostly Likely D and prediction markets still price Democrats around 85-88%. A margin of about four points with wide uncertainty balances the tight recent surveys against the stronger structural and market signals.", "watch": "Any post-October poll showing Tafoya ahead, or further escalation of the fraud issue, would push this into true tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tina Smith (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's open Senate seat has tightened sharply in the final weeks. Polls from late September show Peggy Flanagan leading Michele Tafoya by one to two points, a big shift from summer surveys that had Democrats up five or more. Outside groups have poured millions into attacks on Flanagan, and fraud-related controversies have given Republicans a rare opening in a state that still leans Democratic by about three points.\n\nDespite the tight polling, most professional raters continue to call the race Likely Democratic, and prediction markets put Flanagan's chances in the mid-80s. The race sits between those signals: closer than the fundamentals suggest, but not yet a coin flip. Turnout patterns in the Twin Cities suburbs and greater Minnesota will likely decide it.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8725, "margin": 5.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7776, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8131, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8217, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7867, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.784, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7719, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7956, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7935, "